set_option linter.unusedVariables false

/-!
# A172004

Let y = y(u,v) be implicitly defined by g(u,v,y(u,v)) = 0. Read as a triangle by rows k = 1,2,..., the sequence represents the number of terms a(i,k-i) in the expansion of the partial derivatives d^k y/du^i dv^{k-i} in terms of partial derivatives of g.

The 52 terms known to OEIS, indexed from `1`.

Skeleton generated by `lake exe oeis-gen`; every declaration is a `sorry` placeholder.
-/

namespace A172004

/-- Known terms of `flat`, starting at index `1`. -/
def flatData : List flatRetType :=
  [1, 1, 3, 4, 3, 9, 15, 15, 9, 24,
    47, 59, 47, 24, 61, 136, 195, 195, 136, 61,
    145, 360, 580, 663, 580, 360, 145, 333, 904, 1586,
